{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot perception and motion primitives as a single automaton, capturing all possible sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification enforces safe, coverage-biased exploration: forward/random_walk in clear, rotate_clockwise on left obstacle, rotate_counterclockwise on right obstacle, move_backward on front obstacle, and full_rotate only as a last-resort after repeated blockages. All obstacle events force a recovery state before resuming exploration. Each state enables exactly one controllable action, and uncontrollable events are total in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Unify perception and motion in the plant to reflect open-loop pulse semantics and all possible event orderings.",
    "Specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented action selection, conservative recovery, and rapid return to exploration after clearance."
